# Development scratch. `TASKS.md`, `SHIP.md`, `benchmark.Rmd`, `check.sh` and the
# `survival-*.R` scripts are maintained, so they are kept; the rest is not part
# of the package. In particular `_dev/Reproduce/` is Linero's JASA replication
# package -- seven third-party GPL-2 packages -- which is here as a reference and
# is not ours to redistribute, and `benchmark.html` is regenerable output.
#
# The `survival-*.R` scripts are the provenance of every number in
# `vignette("survival")`, which names them, so they are kept while their `.rds`
# outputs are not: `vignettes/survival-results.rds` is the one that ships.
_dev/*
!_dev/TASKS.md
!_dev/SHIP.md
!_dev/benchmark.Rmd
!_dev/check.sh
!_dev/survival-sim.R
!_dev/survival-bins.R
!_dev/survival-timing.R
!_dev/survival-results.R
!_dev/bcf-interfaces.md
!_dev/bcf-proof.R
!_dev/bcf-mixing.R
!_dev/sigma-mu-mixing.R
!_dev/sigma-mu-cause.R
!_dev/sigma-mu-others.R
!_dev/ate-atom.R
!_dev/sparsity-default.R
!_dev/sparsity-effect-size.R
!_dev/categorical-priors.R
!_dev/categorical-check.R
!_dev/categorical-benchmark.R
!_dev/factor-random-vs-fixed.R
!_dev/bookkeeping-cost.R
!_dev/varying-coefficients.md

